  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two identical simple pendulums, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span>, oscillate with amplitude <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> and period <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>. At <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span>, pendulum <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> is at its maximum positive displacement and pendulum <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> is at its maximum negative displacement.</p>\n<p>Which row correctly identifies the total distance travelled by the bob of pendulum <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> during one complete period and the phase difference between the two oscillations?</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Total distance travelled <br/> in one period</th><th>Phase difference / rad</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-label=\"A\"><td>A.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2A\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\pi\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"B\"><td>B.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4A\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\pi\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"C\"><td>C.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2A\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\\pi\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"D\"><td>D.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4A\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\\pi\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>"
